    "summary": "I built a three-storey tower from north-half bases: a drawer on the bottom storey and an open 2-compartment bin on the top. The final check found no rule errors and no mesh clashes. Drawers can only sit on the cut face of a half base, so I replaced the full base you started with by a half base, and the two storeys above it had to be half bases too. The tower therefore has only one drawer and one bin, each half a cell wide. I left the middle storey empty. The check suggests caps for 11 open faces; I left them off because the brief didn't ask for them."
